+HTCondor Deployments
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+   from dask_jobqueue import HTCondorCluster
+
+   cluster = HTCondorCluster(queue='default',
+                            project='DaskOnHTCondor',
+                            local_directory='$TMPDIR',
+                            cores=24,
+                            processes=6,
+                            memory='16GB',
+                            resource_spec='select=1:ncpus=24:mem=100GB')
+
+   cluster = HTCondorCluster(cores=24,
+                            processes=6,
+                            shebang='#!/usr/bin/env zsh',
+                            memory="6GB",
+                            project='P48500028',
+                            queue='premium',
+                            resource_spec='select=1:ncpus=36:mem=109G',
+                            walltime='02:00:00',
+                            interface='ib0')
+
+To set environment variables in the job script, you can use the ``env_extra`` keyword argument when initializing your cluster object. The behavior of ``env_extra`` is specific to the job queue implementation.
+
